/_engine_support/bridge_fsck_drift.py:31-35` and `bridge_fsck_visibility.py:36-50`. In-process `sys.path.insert(engine_dir)` sites: `_cli/__init__.py:148-151`, `_commands/_repair_pause.py:39-42`, `_commands/doctor_mapping.py:43-45`, `_commands/fsck_repair.py:344-347`. `src/rebar/graph/_loader.py:3` only mentions the idiom historically (no change).\n\n**Scripts (Approach step 6) line cites:** `scripts/check_raw_git_writes.py:143` (`_RECONCILER = Path(\"src/rebar/reconciler\")`), `scripts/check_config_ownership.py:77-85,137`, `scripts/capture_jira_fixtures.py:157-159`, `scripts/generate_dc_wiki_legacy_outputs.py:39-43`, `scripts/jira_dc_capability_map.py:64-82`, `scripts/measure_baseline_normalization.py:67-68,129-130,222`, `scripts/measure_get_rotation_cutover.py:22-24`, `infra/scripts/comment_echo_reclaim_manifest.py:28-30`. Verified as NOT hardcoding the engine dir (untouched): `scripts/check_repo_root_from_package.py`, `scripts/check_repo_root_from_tracker.py`, `scripts/check_tickets_boundary.py`.\n\n**Docs (Approach step 9) line cites:** `docs/user-guide.md:658-661`, `docs/architecture.md:31,72,244-272`, `README.md:289`, `docs/exit-codes.md:55-57`; `docs/code-navigation.md`, `docs/coverage.md`, `docs/config.md`, `docs/reuse-surface.md` (whole-file spelling pass).\n\n**`.github/complexity-baseline.json` (Approach step 10) — the six keys**, re-spelled from `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/...` to `src/rebar/reconciler/...` with ceilings unchanged: `outbound_fields.py::_diff_fields:32`, `applier.py::apply:22`, `binding_walk.py::compute_binding_walk_mutations:27`, `dispatch_one.py::create_one:36`, `inbound_differ.py::_diff_jira_vs_local:16`, `outbound_field_diff.py::diff_canonical_fields:23`. (`.github/mechanism-baseline.json` has 29 `autouse_fixture::tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/...` keys; they are untouched by this story because the test package does not move here — the next story re-spells them.)\n\n**`sys.modules` keys the source registers and tests pre-seed (all deleted by the Approach step 8 codemod):** dotted `rebar_reconciler.{_advisory_lock,mode,request,pass_support,_preflight,alert_store,mutation,config,link_direction,adapters.jira.adf,operation_outcome,failure_policy,git_adapter,observation,create_route,coordinator,ticket_planner,ticket_plan,runtime,retry_budget,reconcile_helpers,rebar_id_audit,persist_phase,pass_io,pass_fuse,manifest_renderer,load_phase,dispatch_one,create_coordinator,create_containment,apply_phase,apply_handlers,applier,_errors,batch_dispatch,binding_store,_ref_lock,_loader,__main__}`; flat keys `reconcile_helpers`, `pass_support`, `reconcile_mutation`, `rebar_reconciler_errors`, `rebar_reconciler__ref_lock_advisory`, `rebar_reconciler_ref_lock_advisory`, `rebar_reconciler_ref_lock_push`, `rebar_reconciler_config`, `rebar_reconciler_alert_store`, `reconcile_selection_binding_store`, `reconcile_run_differs`, `reconcile_config`, `reconcile_classify`, `reconcile_binding_walk`, `_concurrency`, `conflict_resolver`, `config`, `overview`, `rebar._engine_mode`, `rebar_reconciler_classify_fsck`; test-private keys (`applier`, `fetcher`, `reconcile_*`, `rebar_reconciler_advisory_lock`, `rebar_reconciler_mode`, ~60 per-file names). 343 test files / 442 `spec_from_file_location` sites; 149 files `import rebar_reconciler`. `pyproject.toml:691-698` has `testpaths=[\"tests\"]` and no `pythonpath`/`rootdir` — the package rename needs no pytest config change.\n\n**Kept, not deleted (already discharged on origin/main):** `Mode.RECONCILE_CHECK` is absent (`mode.py:39-42`); `_ref_lock.py:717` writer persists `\"dry-run\"` (`_PAUSE_GATED_MODE`, `:591`) and the decoder keeps `_PAUSE_LEGACY_GATED_MODES={\"reconcile-check\"}` (`:592`) — bug `extralegal-durative-beaver` is closed (Gerrit 2728); `mode.py:57` `from_str(\"reconcile-check\")→DRY_RUN` and `_ref_lock.py:592` stay as persisted-pause-blob read compat. `MODE_CAPS` is live (`__main__.py:187`, `apply_planning.py:93`, `load_phase.py:165`, `ticket_planner.py:60`) and the bootstrap modes are live consumers (`reconcile-bridge.yml:59-60`, DC harness `tests/external/live_jira_dc/test_dc_mutations.py:70`, `manifest_renderer.py`) — kept; only the MCP by-path load and the dead `ctx.MODE_CAPS`/`ctx.Mode` handles (`mcp_server.py:599-600`, no registrar reads them) are deleted.\n\n**Release note (BREAKING) for `CHANGELOG.md`:** `python -m rebar_reconciler` becomes `python -m rebar.reconciler`; the top-level `rebar_reconciler` import name is removed with no shim (ADR 0083, ADR 0111); `rebar._engine.engine_env` no longer prepends `PYTHONPATH`.","timestamp":1788807674126973120},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Operator sanction (recorded on the epic): this change carries a value-preserving key re-spell of the `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/...` keys in `.github/complexity-baseline.json` (S1, 6 keys): prefix rewrite only, ceilings and counts unchanged; state this sanction in the commit message.","timestamp":1788807694029980930},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Cross-epic assignment from the docs/ADR epic (astounding-pictural-cowbird): two comments in modules this story moves cite a design document (`docs/designs/sync-hardening-proposal.md`) that never existed in git history. Rewrite them in this change, at the moved paths (origin/main 083620b0 line numbers):\n\n- `inbound_differ.py:265-266`: replace `# Canonical entries (as of 183fd51ac2; pending consolidation into` / `# _field_contract.py per docs/designs/sync-hardening-proposal.md Item 3):` with `# Canonical entries (as of 183fd51ac2; the per-field symmetry rules live in` / `# _field_contract.py, which names this map; consolidation tracked by story a130-2b7c-429c-43d1):`.\n- `apply_handlers.py:504-505`: replace `evidence feeds the binding-GC design in` / `# docs/designs/sync-hardening-proposal.md Item 4b.` with `evidence feeds binding retirement per ADR 0028 (deletion is proven only by a` / `# direct 404; bug 13eb-c414-0763-4fa1 covers GC of bindings to deleted issues).`\n\nBoth replacement blocks stay accepted by `scripts/check_comment_hygiene.py` (grouped-hex ticket ids present). The docs epic's own story fixes the remaining phantom citations in `scripts/` and `tests/`; after both land, `git grep -n 'sync-hardening-proposal'` over `src scripts tests` is empty.","timestamp":1788807986691990359},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"CI-lock fact for the `.github/complexity-baseline.json` re-spell (step 10 of the Approach): the `Complexity-baseline lock` step in `.github/workflows/_build-and-test.yml` runs `python scripts/check_complexity_baseline.py --lock`, which diffs this change's baseline against main's copy at the merge base and rejects ANY added key (`lock_against_base`, `scripts/check_complexity_baseline.py:488-511`: \"NEW entry added ... an administrator must override the gate\"). A path re-spell is a removed key plus an added key, so the lock cannot distinguish it from a smuggled new ceiling and will vote `Verified -1` on this change even though `make lint` (`--check`) and `tests/unit/test_complexity_baseline.py` pass locally. Landing therefore requires the override the lock was designed with (task 47e9): an administrator force-submit of this one change after confirming the lock step is the only red item in its CI run. Agents must not perform that override; the session owner escalates it to the operator. Alternatives considered and rejected: reducing the six functions under the threshold inside a move story (not behaviour-preserving), and teaching the lock about renames (a gate redesign for a one-time move).","timestamp":1788809631417226465},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Operator decision 2026-09-07 (approved): keep the value-preserving re-spell of the six `.github/complexity-baseline.json` keys in this change. Landing instruction: push for review as its own change; when CI reports `Verified -1` with the `Complexity-baseline lock` step as the ONLY red item, the operator (an administrator) force-submits it, which is the override task 47e9 designed the lock with. The implementing agent must not perform the override; it reports the CI run and hands off. The commit message names the six keys, states that ceilings are unchanged, and cites this decision.","timestamp":1788809962492156489},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Experiment result (2026-09-07, scratch worktree at origin/main 4c77d6f3e96f, `git mv src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler src/rebar/reconciler` only, no import edits):\n- C901 scores are path-independent: after the move `--check` reports the six functions as `new` at the new path with scores 32, 20, 27, 27, 16, 23, identical to their scores at the old path on the clean tree; the old keys bucket `stale`. (`apply` at 20 and `create_one` at 27 are already under their ceilings 22 and 36 on main, so they were already stale there.)\n- The re-spell must RE-SORT the ceilings map, not just substitute the prefix: a plain in-place `sed` fails `--check` with `error: 'ceilings' keys must be sorted`, because `src/rebar/reconciler/...` sorts after `src/rebar/_engine_support/...`, `_ids.py`, `_mcp_reads.py` and the other underscore-prefixed keys. Rewrite the file through `render_baseline` (or `json.dumps(..., indent=2, sort_keys=True)` matching its format); `git diff --stat` then shows 6 insertions, 6 deletions.\n- After the sorted re-spell: `--check` gives `active=33 new=0 increased=0 stale=16`, byte-for-byte the clean tree's summary (the 16 stale rows pre-exist on main and are not this story's to drain), and `pytest tests/unit/test_complexity_baseline.py -q` passes (87 passed).\n- The lock against main's copy (`--lock --base <main's baseline>`) prints exactly six `complexity-baseline lock: NEW entry added: 'src/rebar/reconciler/...'` lines plus the administrator hint and exits 1; removed old-path entries are not flagged. This confirms the landing instruction above: the lock step is the one expected red item for the operator's force-submit.\n- `rebar._proc.reap_process_group(proc, *, grace, drain, label, logger)` exists at `src/rebar/_proc.py:38`; two thin `_reap_process_group` wrappers in `adapters/jira/acli_subprocess.py:507` and `jira_family/wiki_render.py:417` import it lazily and move with the package.","timestamp":1788813374091445754},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Coordination note (2026-09-07): open bug unaware-subwealthy-pintail (f778-6dd7-8913-4043, priority 3, reconciler creates a duplicate ticket and Jira issue when a bound pair loses both its binding and its `rebar-id` label) will be fixed inside `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/` modules this story moves. Landing order: either that fix lands before this move (then this story carries it across), or it lands after and is authored against `src/rebar/reconciler/`. A fix in flight during the move must be rebased by its author; `git mv` history keeps `git log --follow` working for the moved files.","timestamp":1788813867955287894},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Plan-review round 1 (2026-09-07, BLOCK) findings folded into the revised description: `_commands/bridge_repair.py:158-160` (`_engine_module(\"rebar_reconciler.binding_store\")`) was in Scope with no described rewrite (step 5 now names it); prose references at `timeutils.py:9,11`, `_proc.py:7`, `_operation_config.py:232` and `_bridge_commands.py:32` plus the bare argv string at `_bridge_commands.py:51` were outside the codemod patterns (step 1 now covers bare tokens and quoted names, and those files are in Scope); two `__main__.py` cites were wrong (`install_stderr_handler` is at `:491`, the reconcile-absent no-op branch at `:344-348`; the `_advisory is None` fallback at `:364-371` and the `_load_sibling_keyed`/`_try_load_step` helpers at `:116-160` with call sites `:315,344,358,367,417,493,494,529` are now named); the docs grep is now an explicit edge check. The reviewer also flagged the unit as large for one session (advisory); the operator's force-submit landing instruction stands, so the change stays whole.","timestamp":1788814684537194345},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Plan-review round 2 (2026-09-07, BLOCK) folded into the revised description: `src/rebar/_config_sections.py:153,208` (two prose references) and the path literal at `src/rebar/llm/eval_specs/plan-review-asserted-capability.eval.yaml:81` are in step 1's rewrite set and in Scope, with `_config_sections.py`'s non-prose lines assigned to the config epic; the basis sentence now names 4c77d6f3e96f for the `__main__.py` cites.","timestamp":1788816950554208887},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Coordination update: colliding bug fix unaware-subwealthy-pintail has landed and closed. Gerrit change 2834 merged as 02e0fae923d45329a3e1dc1921d70e19484401b8 (Use Jira property for dedup). The package-move epic can now rebase/carry the reconciler changes from the current module paths.","timestamp":1788888306036654001},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Revision 2, by lane ebf5 on 2026-10-19 against origin/main c0cf1022671. The description was rewritten. This comment carries the enumerations the description points to, and it replaces the first comment wherever the two differ.\n\n**What changed from revision 1, and why**\nRe-review on c0cf1022671 returned BLOCK. Seven findings were folded in:\n- (1) `tests/unit/test_engine_dir.py` needs edits beyond `:27`.\n- (2) `infra/scripts/comment_echo_reclaim_manifest.py:28-39` has a by-path loader. It is a sibling of `_engine`, so it now imports `rebar.reconciler.inbound_fields`.\n- (3) Five test modules import `_lib_ops._engine_module`.\n- (4) `scripts/check_mcp_library_parity.py` no longer exists (deleted by masonic-excusable-guppy). Only `scripts/gen_mcp_reference.py:96-97` carries the kwargs.\n- (5) Rollback is now stated.\n- (6) The disposition of the deleted fallbacks is now stated.\n- (7) The 2 advisory items: the AC is split, and size stays as one story because a package rename cannot land half-done.\n\nCoordinator decision applied: `pyproject.toml` is untouched, and T201 is handled with inline `# noqa: T201`. Follow-up likable-waterworn-willet (ab45-2cb2-c1b6-4c5b) records `discovered_from` this story and `depends_on` f7dc-132b-057a-476c; that edge was escalated to the epic.\n`docs/exit-codes.md` is no longer touched: main's c0cf1022671 already removed its reconciler path.\n\n**Out-of-package src callers**\n- `_lib_ops.py`: `_engine_module` deleted. Callers use `importlib.import_module(\"rebar.reconciler.{projects_store,pass_support,__main__,mode,last_pass,_ref_lock,access_check}\")`.\n- `_bridge_runner.py:147-151`\n- `_commands/bridge_repair.py:158-160`\n- `_cli/_bridge_commands.py`: `_ref_lock_module` deleted along with its `_status` call. The `-m rebar.reconciler` argv is at `:50`.\n- `mcp_server.py`: `_load_engine_mode` and `MODE_CAPS, Mode` deleted, plus the `ctx.MODE_CAPS` / `ctx.Mode` entries. The handle kwargs are dropped in `scripts/gen_mcp_reference.py`, `tests/unit/test_gen_mcp_reference.py`, `tests/unit/test_cross_session_mcp.py`, and `tests/unit/test_mcp_plan_review_status.py`.\n- Plain imports replace the `sys.path.insert` sites in `_cli/__init__.py`, `_commands/_repair_pause.py`, `_commands/doctor_mapping.py`, and `_commands/fsck_repair.py`.\n- Plain imports replace the loaders in `_engine_support/bridge_fsck_drift.py` (classify) and `_engine_support/bridge_fsck_visibility.py` (access_check).\n- `src/rebar/_engine/jira-capability-probe.py`: import path.\n- `src/rebar/_engine.py`: `engine_env` and its docstrings.\n\n**Prose-only src edits**\n- `timeutils.py`, `_proc.py`, `_operation_config.py`, `_logging.py`, `_config_schema.py`, `_config_sections.py`, `_config_sources.py`\n- `_store/push_state.py`, `schemas/__init__.py`\n- `llm/eval_specs/plan-review-asserted-capability.eval.yaml`\n\n**In-package loader sites rewritten**\n- Prologues deleted in every module that had one.\n- Hand-rolled loaders: `applier._load_concurrency`, `differ._load_sibling`/`_load_mutation`, `fetcher` alert_store, `inbound_collection_diffs`, `inbound_fields`, `inbound_translate`, `invariants` (alert_store, sink), `last_pass._load_ref_lock`, `binding_repository` alert_store, `outbound_pass` mutation_payloads, `pass_io` (conflict_resolver, alert_store).\n- The `_load(name, relpath)` helpers in `reconcile`, `run_differs`, `pass_support`, `outbound_pass`, and `reconcile_helpers` are now `import_module` seams.\n- `__main__._load_sibling_keyed` and `_try_load_step` are `import_module` seams.\n\n**Type fixes**\n- `adapters/jira/acli.py`: `AcliClient.update_issue(jira_key → remote_id)`. All 43 call sites pass it positionally.\n- `apply_inbound_events._inbound_create_writeback_jira`: `client: TicketTransport | None`.\n- `adapters/jira/summary_operation.py` and `adapters/jira_datacenter/summary_executor.py`: `doc: dict[str, Any]`.\n- `adapters/jira_datacenter/_hierarchy.py`: `cached: Any`.\n- `pass_io.mutate(data: MutableMapping[str, Any])`\n- `outbound_mutation_builders.py`: asserts on `config.jira_snapshot` and `config.absent_alive_fields`. `compute_outbound_mutations` populates both before the loop.\n- `manifest_renderer`: unconditional `retry_budget` import.\n\n**Scripts**\n- `capture_jira_fixtures.py`: drops its `sys.path.insert` and imports `rebar.reconciler.adapters.jira.{acli,acli_subprocess}`.\n- Re-pointed to the new path: `check_cli_json_js_safe.py`, `check_config_ownership.py`, `check_fcntl_import_guard.py`, `check_raw_git_writes.py`, `generate_dc_wiki_legacy_outputs.py`, `jira_dc_capability_map.py`, `measure_baseline_normalization.py`, `measure_get_rotation_cutover.py`.\n- `jira-pressure-test/{README.md,e2e_field_validation_probe.sh,e2e_validation_probe.sh}`: the `.sh` adf by-path load becomes an import.\n\n**Docs**\n`architecture`, `bug-creation-contract`, `code-navigation`, `concurrency`, `config`, `env-vars` (regenerated), `event-schema`, `jira-dc-capability-map`, `mapping-seam`, `migrations`, `release-notes` (a new BREAKING entry only; history is unedited), `remediation-implementation-plan`, `reuse-surface`, `user-guide`, plus `README.md` and `CHANGELOG.md`.\n\n**Tests deleted or rewritten** (all other test edits are mechanical)\n- `tests/unit/test_engine_dir.py`:\n  - The `:27` assertion is removed.\n  - `test_library_path_exposes_no_generic_top_level_engine_names` asserts that `rebar_reconciler` is not importable.\n  - `test_engine_submodules_resolve_when_the_tests_unit_shadow_is_active` is rewritten as `test_engine_submodules_resolve_from_a_tests_unit_module`.\n- `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/orchestrate/test_main_entry.py::test_run_pass_returns_0_when_all_steps_absent` is deleted: it pinned the removed no-op.\n- `test_jira_family_boundary_heldout.py`: the `_loader.py`-exists contract now says it is deleted.\n- `test_arg_sweep_kwargs_heldout.py`: paths updated.\n- `test_transport_param_typing_cc77.py`: the absolute `rebar.reconciler._backend` spelling now resolves. The test still fails on the bare and `Any` spellings.\n- `tests/_engine_path.py`, `tests/conftest.py::_one_engine_root`, and `tests/unit/test_engine_root_convention.py` are adjusted to `src/rebar/reconciler` and stay in place; S2 deletes them.\n\n**Complexity re-spell** (6 keys, ceilings unchanged)\nOld → new prefix: `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/` → `src/rebar/reconciler/`.\n- `adapters/jira/outbound_fields.py::_diff_fields` 32\n- `applier.py::apply` 22\n- `binding_walk.py::compute_binding_walk_mutations` 27\n- `dispatch_one.py::create_one` 36\n- `inbound_differ.py::_diff_jira_vs_local` 16\n- `outbound_field_diff.py::diff_canonical_fields` 23\n\n`--check` reports `active=28 new=0 increased=0 stale=21`.\n\n**Measured so far on the scratch implementation**\n- `make typecheck`: \"Success: no issues found in 750 source files\".\n- Lint, the complexity check, and the mechanism check are green. The mechanism counts are `new=26` (all admitted) and `increased=0`, identical to main.\n- `ruff check --select T201 --isolated src/rebar/reconciler` reports 0 findings.\n- `gen_env_registry.py --check` is clean.\n- The test conversion is in progress.","timestamp":1792428965282825940}],"created_at":1788807372317960637,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[],"description":"## Context / Problem\n`src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/` is package data imported by path: `_loader.py::lazy_load`, the in-package loader prologues and hand-rolled sibling loaders, and out-of-package loaders (`_lib_ops._engine_module`, `_bridge_commands._ref_lock_module`, `mcp_server._load_engine_mode`, `infra/scripts/comment_echo_reclaim_manifest.py:28-39`, four `sys.path.insert` sites, `_engine.engine_env`'s PYTHONPATH prepend). The generic top-level name breaks namespace hygiene, the by-path idiom forces a `sys.modules` key contract onto ~340 test files, and mypy widens every `rebar_reconciler.`-imported annotation to `Any`. Operator decision (2026-09-06), BREAKING: the package becomes `rebar.reconciler` with no shim (ADR 0083, ADR 0111). Cites are on origin/main c0cf1022671; the enumerated sites and file lists are in the revision-2 comment.\n\n## Approach\n1. `git mv src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler src/rebar/reconciler`; a throwaway codemod over `src`, `scripts`, `infra`, `tests`, docs and `README.md` rewrites imports, quoted keys, path joins (the package is now the engine dir's sibling), private `rebar_reconciler_<x>` cache keys and prose. The test directories `tests/{unit,integration}/rebar_reconciler/` keep their names (next story).\n2. In-package: delete `_loader.py`; every loader prologue and by-path sibling loader becomes `importlib.import_module(\"rebar.reconciler.<mod>\")` or a plain import, keeping loader function names so patch targets survive. `__main__.py` keeps `_load_sibling_keyed`/`_try_load_step` as patchable seams over `import_module` and drops its `rebar` bootstrap fallback. Two runtime fallbacks are pure by-path artifacts and are deleted: the reconcile-absent no-op and `_advisory = None` on `ImportError` (likewise `manifest_renderer`'s `retry_budget` fallback). Every module ships inside the package, so the disposition for a genuinely missing module is a hard `ImportError` at import, exit 1 (the existing unrecoverable-error contract), never a silent converged pass. The stderr handler installs on `rebar`; the package NullHandler goes (the `rebar` root has one).\n3. `engine_env` drops the PYTHONPATH prepend and only pins `REBAR_ROOT`; `engine_dir()` stays for `jira-capability-probe.py` and `resources/`.\n4. Out-of-package callers import directly: delete `_lib_ops._engine_module` (src callers and the five test modules that import it switch to `import_module`), `_bridge_commands._ref_lock_module`, and `mcp_server._load_engine_mode` with the unread `ctx.MODE_CAPS`/`ctx.Mode` handles (and their kwargs in `scripts/gen_mcp_reference.py` and three tests); the `sys.path.insert` sites and the `_engine_support/bridge_fsck_{drift,visibility}.py` and infra-script loaders become plain imports.\n5. Scripts that hardcode the directory are re-pointed.\n6. `pyproject.toml` is NOT edited: any edit trips the Gerrit pip-audit dependency-map lane on the open advisories (unhelpful-supersmart-chrysalis). The old T201 glob stays as a dead entry; the 99 reconciler `print()` sites get inline `# noqa: T201` (`ruff check --select T201 --add-noqa`); follow-up likable-waterworn-willet moves the glob once the advisories clear.\n7. Type fixes the now-resolvable types surface, no behaviour change: `AcliClient.update_issue`'s first parameter renamed `remote_id` to match the `TicketTransport` port (no keyword caller), and a few annotations/`assert is not None` (comment).\n8. Tests, mechanical: by-path helpers become `import_module`; `sys.modules` seeds, namespace stubs, engine-dir constants and `sys.path.insert` go; the module-level shadow-package bridges in `tests/unit/conftest.py` and `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/conftest.py` go (fixtures stay); private module copies become `monkeypatch.setattr` on the shared module (no `importlib.reload`). `tests/_engine_path.py`, `_one_engine_root` and `test_engine_root_convention.py` stay, adjusted to `src/rebar/reconciler` (next story deletes them). Rewritten or deleted tests are listed in the comment.\n9. Docs: maintained docs and `README.md` spell `rebar.reconciler`; `docs/architecture.md`'s package-layout section describes the new layout; BREAKING entries in `CHANGELOG.md` and `docs/release-notes.md`; regenerate `docs/env-vars.md`.\n10. `.github/complexity-baseline.json`: re-spell the 6 engine keys under `ceilings` to `src/rebar/reconciler/...`, ceilings unchanged, written through `render_baseline` (sorted). Operator-sanctioned; the CI `Complexity-baseline lock` step rejects the six added keys by design and the operator force-submits (landing instruction in the comments).\nRollback: one atomic commit (rename, codemod, re-spell); `git revert` restores `rebar_reconciler`, every loader, the PYTHONPATH prepend and the six old keys together. No expand-contract window: the old name is never importable beside the new one.\n\n## Scope\n`src/rebar/reconciler/**` (moved), the out-of-package callers and prose sites listed in the revision-2 comment, the scripts and infra script there, `.github/complexity-baseline.json`, tests per step 8, the maintained `docs/*.md` listed there, `README.md`, `CHANGELOG.md`. Out of scope: `pyproject.toml` (step 6), the rest of `_cli/` (CLI epic), the test-side loader complex and test-package rename (next story), any engine behaviour change.\n\n## Testing\n`python -c \"import rebar.reconciler, rebar.reconciler.__main__\"`; `python -m rebar.reconciler --help` exits 0 with no PYTHONPATH; `pytest tests/unit/rebar_reconciler tests/interfaces tests/scripts -q`; `make typecheck`; `python scripts/check_complexity_baseline.py --check` prints `new=0 increased=0`; `ruff check --select T201 --isolated src/rebar/reconciler` is clean. Edge greps: `git grep -nE 'rebar_reconciler' -- src scripts infra` and the same over `docs README.md ':!docs/adr' ':!docs/experiments' ':!docs/archive' ':!docs/release-notes.md'` return only references to the not-yet-renamed `tests/{unit,integration}/rebar_reconciler` test paths (historical release-note entries keep the name they shipped under).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/` and `_loader.py` do not exist and `src/rebar/reconciler/__init__.py` exists (`git ls-tree`).\n- [ ] `git grep -nE 'spec_from_file_location|lazy_load\\(' -- src infra` returns only the `src/rebar/graph/_loader.py` docstring.\n- [ ] Both edge greps in Testing match nothing beyond the listed exceptions.\n- [ ] `python -m rebar.reconciler preview --repo-root <tmp>` runs from a fresh venv with no `PYTHONPATH` (`tests/interfaces/facades/test_bridge_cli_heldout.py` subprocess case).\n- [ ] `make verify` exits 0 apart from the known arm64 pandoc host failures.\n- [ ] `check_complexity_baseline.py --check` prints `new=0 increased=0` with the 6 sorted `src/rebar/reconciler/` keys at unchanged ceilings.\n- [ ] `ruff check --select T201 --isolated src/rebar/reconciler` reports nothing and `pyproject.toml` is unchanged.\n- [ ] `python scripts/gen_env_registry.py --check` is clean.","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/reconciler/","reason":"package moved from _engine, loaders deleted"},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/","reason":"removed"},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine.py","reason":"engine_env drops PYTHONPATH"},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/jira-capability-probe.py","reason":"import path"},{"path":"src/rebar/_lib_ops.py","reason":"delete _engine_module"},{"path":"src/rebar/_bridge_runner.py","reason":"import _Disposition directly"},{"path":"src/rebar/mcp_server.py","reason":"delete _load_engine_mode + ctx.MODE_CAPS/Mode"},{"path":"src/rebar/_cli/__init__.py","reason":"lines 144-151 plain import"},{"path":"src/rebar/_cli/_bridge_commands.py","reason":"delete _ref_lock_module; -m rebar.reconciler"},{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/_repair_pause.py","reason":"plain import"},{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/doctor_mapping.py","reason":"plain import"},{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/fsck_repair.py","reason":"plain import"},{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/bridge_repair.py","reason":"plain import"},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine_support/bridge_fsck_drift.py","reason":"plain import"},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine_support/bridge_fsck_visibility.py","reason":"plain import"},{"path":"src/rebar/_logging.py","reason":"docstring"},{"path":"src/rebar/_config_schema.py","reason":"comment :665 only"},{"path":"pyproject.toml","reason":"T201 glob + comments"},{"path":"scripts/check_raw_git_writes.py","reason":"path"},{"path":"scripts/check_config_ownership.py","reason":"path"},{"path":"scripts/capture_jira_fixtures.py","reason":"path"},{"path":"scripts/generate_dc_wiki_legacy_outputs.py","reason":"path"},{"path":"scripts/jira_dc_capability_map.py","reason":"path"},{"path":"scripts/measure_baseline_normalization.py","reason":"path"},{"path":"scripts/measure_get_rotation_cutover.py","reason":"path"},{"path":"scripts/check_mcp_library_parity.py","reason":"drop kwargs"},{"path":"scripts/gen_mcp_reference.py","reason":"drop kwargs"},{"path":"infra/scripts/comment_echo_reclaim_manifest.py","reason":"path"},{"path":".github/complexity-baseline.json","reason":"6 keys re-spelled, ceilings unchanged (operator-sanctioned)"},{"path":"tests/","reason":"mechanical import codemod (343 files)"},{"path":"docs/user-guide.md","reason":"-m rebar.reconciler"},{"path":"docs/architecture.md","reason":"package name"},{"path":"docs/exit-codes.md","reason":"path"},{"path":"docs/code-navigation.md","reason":"path"},{"path":"docs/coverage.md","reason":"path"},{"path":"docs/config.md","reason":"path"},{"path":"docs/reuse-surface.md","reason":"path"},{"path":"docs/env-vars.md","reason":"regenerated"},{"path":"README.md","reason":":289"},{"path":"CHANGELOG.md","reason":"BREAKING entry"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[["parent","ebf5-5d21-0124-4313"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"ebf5-5d21-0124-4313","parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":["complexity-reduction","breaking-pass-4"],"ticket_id":"bf96-5776-6a97-420f","ticket_type":"story","title":"Move the reconciler to rebar.reconciler and delete every by-path loader","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["48336c0c-71c0-43e1-9f35-a41ec410bec5","769a53e9-22e0-4497-85a2-cd22bcbce005","2962e2c1-3e71-4321-96a4-933e5cd12d3d","9b62d2ca-ee83-4591-9143-16ee04d6a7d0","b6a20712-6ca5-42a4-948a-bc19abcfffe0","fe6b74c8-d52d-42c9-a843-2931cd20b132","800e67a4-d8a8-48e9-8bb2-05b2ea7f52c6","be87d09c-bff9-4fb7-98b8-d9ee9070c79b","25cffe04-e1a7-4434-9422-4a3b822c1ce6","30fd5951-997f-4df5-b931-fdb90863297e","d6f61b35-16fb-47a5-b6c1-c9fa05faf64b"]},"env_id":"","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1792433751226971558,"uuid":"6bf78a95-56a4-4020-8950-77f66c371d14"}